ce":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:e167dbdb23d859d6fd1305c72201ac2b58669e1c8edd7ce66406c00295db6209","file":"preprints/Product-projection-localization-and-the-QAC0-parity-lower-bound-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":25,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"e4371ddc0f57ebf7be4c4de560208d4b57faf68b9812af0e20d6241efc4b6787","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Product-projection-localization-and-the-QAC0-parity-lower-bound-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:e167dbdb23d859d6fd1305c72201ac2b58669e1c8edd7ce66406c00295db6209","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Product-projection-localization-and-the-QAC0-parity-lower-bound-September-24-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L25"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:parity}\nFix a nonnegative integer \\(d\\), a real number \\(c\\ge1\\), and\n\\(0<\\varepsilon\\le1/2\\). For all sufficiently large \\(n\\), no circuit\nof depth at most \\(d\\) on \\(n\\) input qubits and at most \\(n^c\\) total\nqubits, using arbitrary one-qubit unitaries and unbounded-arity Toffoli\ngates, computes \\(\\parity(x)\\) with probability at least\n\\(1/2+\\varepsilon\\) for every \\(x\\in\\{0,1\\}^n\\).\nGates in each layer have disjoint supports, ancillas start in \\(\\ket0\\),\nand one output qubit is measured; the other qubits may be discarded."}
